	abstract = {This paper presents a multi-objective AutoML algorithm to optimize the architecture and hyperparameters of deep SHM models while maximizing the accuracy of networks and minimizing their size and processing burden. It applies reinforcement learning to learn and use the most suitable metaheuristic search operators for different types of variables and various states of optimization through a new data structure called the Q-tensor. The algorithm is applied to two main problems of computer vision-based SHM: damage classification of steel and concrete surfaces. Based on the results, the proposed method outperforms well-established NSGA-II as well as the chain-shaped DCNNs. Moreover, this method provides users with a diverse set of optimized DCNNs that can be chosen based on specific applications, such as offline, real-time, and IoT embedded systems. © 2024 Elsevier B.V.},
