	abstract = {Geopolymer is an environmentally friendly material that is recognized as a potential alternative binder to ordinary Portland cement. However, accurate prediction of the properties of geopolymer composites (GC) has been a concerned issue since there are few design codes for GC to guide their designs. The application of geopolymer has prompted scholars to seek reliable models for predicting their properties, which can save on research costs. With the development of computer science, an increasing number of algorithms are gradually applied to the prediction of GC in recent years. In the present paper, a comprehensive review of the modeling and prediction on GC properties is discussed and the common modeling and prediction methods are introduced in brief, including regression analysis, artificial neural network, adaptive network-based fuzzy inference system, and gene expression programming. Moreover, the advantages, weaknesses, and performance of various methods mentioned in this study are also critically discussed and analyzed. Most methods have presented success in a variety of property forecasts with reliable accuracy, even if the relationships between the properties and the inputs (such as mixture constituents and the curing conditions) are intricate. Nevertheless, these modeling and prediction methods still have some problems in large-scale applications. The effectiveness of these modeling and prediction methods is highly dependent on the database size and the choice of parameter. This review provides a basis for future research on the property modeling and prediction of GC, which could help the researchers and engineers choose the appropriate methods for modeling and prediction of the properties, and to design and optimize the formulations of GC. © 2024 Elsevier Ltd},
